                                25-136
                            </td>
                            <td>
                                SKETCH PLAN - MAYBERRY - A request by Mayberry Communities, LLC for approval of a 631.4-acre Sketch Plan consisting of approximately 383.9 acres allocated toward residential uses, approximately 53.9 acres allocated toward commercial uses, approximately 1.9 acres allocated toward a fire station, approximately 99.1 acres allocated toward open space, parks, trails, drainage, and landscape buffers, and approximately 97.2 acres allocated toward roads and rights-of-way. At full build-out, the maximum development potential contemplated within the Sketch Plan area consists of 2,800 dwelling units, a maximum potential gross density of 4.4 dwelling units per acre, and a maximum of 15.07 acres of commercial development. The property is zoned PUD (Planned Unit Development), CS (Commercial Service), and A-35 (Agricultural) and is located on the south side of US Highway 94, approximately 1.75 miles east of Peyton Highway. The item was heard on the regular agenda at the April 17, 2025 Planning Commission meeting, and was recommended for approval with a vote of 7-0. (Parcel Nos. 3400000456, 3400000460, 3400000472, 3400000474, 3400000476, 3400000477, 3400000478, 3400000479, 3400000480, 3400000495, 3414107001, 3414107002, 3414201024, 3414205001, and 3414217001) (Commissioner District No. 4) (SKP-23-006)
